In Javascript land we defined a symbol `XkcdFilter`. Now we can use it directly when evaluating `Plot`

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Plot[{x, x x, x x x, Sin[x 10]}, {x,0,1}, Prolog->{
  XkcdFilter[
    "wobble" -> 9.6,
    "roughness" -> 0.018,
    "inkBleed" -> 0.55,
    "paperGrain" -> 0.01
  ]
}]

